# Build context for this micro-frontend. `yarn build` runs inside the
# prompt-clients-base image, which already carries the installed workspace
# node_modules, so nothing host-generated may enter this context.
#
# Contents are intentionally identical for clients/core and every
# clients/*_component. Keep them in sync.
#
# DO NOT add: package.json, rspack.config.mjs, src, public, routes, sidebar,
# tailwind.config.js, postcss.config.js, .yarnrc.yml, tsconfig.json,
# components.json, or docker-entrypoint.sh - all of those are read by the build
# or by the final nginx stage.

# Host installs and tool caches. rspack is configured with
# `cache: { type: 'persistent' }`, which writes to node_modules/.cache/rspack -
# 250 MB to 850 MB per component on a developer machine.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.cache
**/.cache

# Build output. Regenerated by `yarn build`.
build
**/build
dist
**/dist
coverage

# VCS / editor / OS noise
.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# No .env file is read at build time (runtime config is injected through
# public/env.template.js + envsubst), so a developer's local one must not leak in.
.env
.env.*
